        "description": "fix: the shell-entry guard notices .devman/writes.toml \u2014 the local layer was inert\n\nFOUND BY TESTING IT, NOT BY A UNIT TEST, and the reason is worth recording: both\nhalves were individually correct.\n\n`resolve_writes()` read `.devman/writes.toml` and merged it over the group's\ndeclaration exactly as designed \u2014 verified directly, the function returns the\nright answer. But the registry entry never changed, because NOTHING MARKED THE\nPROJECTION STALE when that file was edited. The renderer was never asked to run.\n\nWHY `plan` EQUALITY CANNOT COVER IT. Which files are in a working tree is a\nrun-time fact, so the local layer is read by the renderer rather than by Nix \u2014\nthe same reason `.devman/workflows/` and `.devman/triggers.toml` are. The guard\nnotices an edit to a local file the only way it can: by comparing the\nrepository's copy against the verbatim copy the last projection kept beside the\nentry (S-5a). 015 shipped the layer with neither half of that.\n\nSo this adds both, mirroring the trigger layer exactly:\n  - `apply()` keeps `.devman/writes.toml` beside the entry, and removes the kept\n    copy when the source goes;\n  - the guard compares the two, and marks the projection stale on any\n    difference, including appearance and disappearance.\n\nMEASURED END TO END, ON THE LIVE PLANE, after the rebuild that deployed 0.4.0:\n  - declare `[format] tier = \"free\", paths = [\"src/**\"]` in `.devman/writes.toml`\n  - enter the shell -> entry becomes {\"format\": {\"tier\": \"free\", ...}}\n  - `devman doctor` -> \"!! writes  devman/format: tier free over src/** \u2014\n    outside agent surface\", exit 1\n  - remove the file, enter the shell -> entry back to the group's insitu\n    declaration, kept copy gone, doctor exit 0\n\nBefore this commit every step of that sequence was a no-op.\n\nThree regression tests, covering the two halves and the property they exist for:\nthe kept copy is written, it is removed with its source, and what the repository\ndeclares is what the registry records.\n\nGates: base:check 0, base:test 0, doctor 0, pytest 417 passed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
