        "description": "fix(changelog): the summary workflow crosses no import boundary\n\n`groups/changelog/workflows/changelog.yaml` could not run. Two steps imported\npyjutsu inside `devenv shell -- python3`, and a third reached templateer\nthrough an interpreter search-path variable at an absolute sibling checkout.\n\nA console script is a property of the machine; a library import is a property\nof the interpreter that imports it. The shared toolchain venv lends `gitman`\nand `templateer` through PATH, and PATH cannot lend a library through\n`sys.path`. Measured: `devenv shell -- python3 -c 'import pyjutsu'` fails and\n`devenv shell -- gitman` works, while both repoman doctor and gitman doctor\nreport pyjutsu green \u2014 each asks its own interpreter, neither asks the step's\n(023-toolchain P1, P2).\n\n- gate and write call `gitman log --revset <a>..<b> --json` (023 phase 2a).\n  The remaining python3 is standard library only.\n- summarize calls `templateer` by name off PATH.\n- the gate probes for both tools first, inside the same `devenv shell --`\n  every later command uses.\n- TEMPLATEER_TEMPLATE_PATH is repository-relative; groups/README.md forbids a\n  group workflow from holding an absolute path. 022's open question 2 stays\n  open and is now stated where an adopter reads it.\n- the generation is read as a structured result and a failed one is refused.\n  templateer does not forward finish_reason, and its own validator forbids a\n  success carrying no artifact, so P6's truncation surfaces as failure_reason.\n  A second check refuses a whitespace-only artifact, which the schema permits.\n- `--model openai:$GPU_LLM_MODEL`. Measured: `--model gemma` returns\n  failure_reason config_error, 'Unknown model: gemma'.\n- one `devenv shell --` per step, not four across two (M2: 0.755 s warm).\n\nAlso repairs two files that held a raw unified diff body rather than its\nresult, adds the writes.toml the group README already promised, and records\nrevision 5 in DESIGN.md.\n\nchangelog-entries.yaml is NOT converted: it needs diffs and gitman has no diff\nverb. The post-land chain does not run. Stated in the group README.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
