        "description": "docs(stage-7): the atuout reconciler branch \u2014 salvaged, and the stale entry measured\n\nOption A, executed. The 427-line out-of-process reconciler suite is on atuout\nmain; the branch, its remote and the worktree are gone; devman doctor --prune\nremoved the registry entry.\n\nThe salvage found a bug. On main the suite fails 7 of 22 runs, and the cause is\nnot the test: run() starts two threads that each call store.connect(), and\nPRAGMA journal_mode=WAL races on a DB that does not exist yet. When the tail\nthread loses, the reconciler removes its pidfile and exits on first boot.\nMeasured 37/200 fresh, 0/200 existing. Fixed on atuout (6046f4f); 15/15 after.\n\nThe registry lifecycle is now measured, not assumed: the entry does not\nself-remove, a sibling's shell entry does not clear it, and the 00:05 maintain\nstays scheduled until doctor --prune unprojects it. CONCEPT \u00a79.3 predicted all\nthree.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
